# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# The little switch on the Deskbar's tray, which has THREE seats: light,
# without hue, and dark.  A press walks to the next one and round, writes
# the DarkMode setting down, and the whole desktop is repainted out of
# whichever table that names.  The switch IS the setting: the same sync
# path the Preferences control uses answers here.
wait 12
note the backdrop is the Be blue while the switch sits at the left
expect-pixel 300 500 336698
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings DarkMode
note one press: dark, and the setting is written as a NUMBER now, since
note the switch stopped being a flag the moment it grew a third seat
click 933 82
wait 25
expect-pixel 300 500 1c2a3a
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings DarkMode 1
note a second press: no hue anywhere, and the backdrop is a plain grey
click 933 82
wait 25
expect-pixel 300 500 707070
expect-file-has /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings DarkMode 2
note and a third comes back round to where it started, which is why the
note press walks rather than toggling: three seats and one button
click 933 82
wait 25
expect-pixel 300 500 336698
expect-file-lacks /tmp/trk_home/.config/TrackerSettings DarkMode
